File: ForeignFunctions.info, Node: Top, Up: (dir)

ForeignFunctions -- foreign function interface
**********************************************

Description
===========

This package provides the ability to load and call "foreign" functions from
shared libraries and to convert back and forth between Macaulay2 things and the
foreign objects used by these functions.  It is powered by libffi (see
https://sourceware.org/libffi/ ).

As a simple example, we call the cos function from the C standard library,
which sends a double (a real number represented as a double-precision floating
point number) to another double, the cosine of the input.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : mycos = foreignFunction("cos", double, double)|
|                                                   |
|o1 = cos                                           |
|                                                   |
|o1 : ForeignFunction                               |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : mycos pi                                      |
|                                                   |
|o2 = -1                                            |
|                                                   |
|o2 : ForeignObject of type double                  |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : value oo                                      |
|                                                   |
|o3 = -1                                            |
|                                                   |
|o3 : RR (of precision 53)                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+

In this example, we created a ForeignFunction object using the *note
foreignFunction: foreignFunction, constructor method and specified that both
its output and input were instances of the *note double: ForeignRealType, type,
which is one of several *note ForeignType: ForeignType, objects that are
available.

See also the following additional examples:

  * *note fast Fourier transform example: fast Fourier transform example, --
    fast Fourier transforms using foreign function calls to the FFTW library
  * *note general linear model example: general linear model example, --
    constrained least squares using foreign function calls to the LAPACK
    library
  * *note just-in-time compilation example: just-in-time compilation example,
    -- using foreign function calls for computing Fibonacci numbers using JIT
