ForeignPointerArrayType -- foreign type for NULL-terminated arrays of pointers
******************************************************************************

Description
===========

This is the class for a particular kind of array type, where the entries of
each array are some sort of pointer type and the lengths are arbitrary. There
are two built-in types, charstarstar (for arrays of strings) and voidstarstar
(for arrays of pointers), but more types may be constructed using *note
foreignPointerArrayType: foreignPointerArrayType,.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : charstarstar {"foo", "bar", "baz"}                                   |
|                                                                          |
|o1 = {foo, bar, baz}                                                      |
|                                                                          |
|o1 : ForeignObject of type char**                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : charstarstar {"the", "quick", "brown", "fox", "jumps", "over", "the",|
|         "lazy", "dog"}                                                   |
|                                                                          |
|o2 = {the, quick, brown, fox, jumps, over, the, lazy, dog}                |
|                                                                          |
|o2 : ForeignObject of type char**                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : voidstarstar {address int 0, address int 1, address int 2}           |
|                                                                          |
|o3 = {0x7fb3b719ad20, 0x7fb3b719ad10, 0x7fb3b719ad00}                     |
|                                                                          |
|o3 : ForeignObject of type void**                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Foreign pointer arrays may be subscripted using *note _: (Macaulay2Doc)_us,.

+-------------------------------------------+
|i4 : x = charstarstar {"foo", "bar", "baz"}|
|                                           |
|o4 = {foo, bar, baz}                       |
|                                           |
|o4 : ForeignObject of type char**          |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i5 : x_1                                   |
|                                           |
|o5 = bar                                   |
|                                           |
|o5 : ForeignObject of type char*           |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i6 : x_(-1)                                |
|                                           |
|o6 = baz                                   |
|                                           |
|o6 : ForeignObject of type char*           |
+-------------------------------------------+

Their lengths may be found using *note length: (Macaulay2Doc)length,.

+-------------+
|i7 : length x|
|             |
|o7 = 3       |
+-------------+

They are also *note iterable: (Macaulay2Doc)iterator,.

+---------------------------------+
|i8 : i = iterator x;             |
+---------------------------------+
|i9 : next i                      |
|                                 |
|o9 = foo                         |
|                                 |
|o9 : ForeignObject of type char* |
+---------------------------------+
|i10 : next i                     |
|                                 |
|o10 = bar                        |
|                                 |
|o10 : ForeignObject of type char*|
+---------------------------------+
|i11 : scan(x, print)             |
|foo                              |
|bar                              |
|baz                              |
+---------------------------------+

They may also be modified using subscripted assignment.

+----------------------------------+
|i12 : x_0 = "qux"                 |
|                                  |
|o12 = qux                         |
|                                  |
|o12 : ForeignObject of type char* |
+----------------------------------+
|i13 : x                           |
|                                  |
|o13 = {qux, bar, baz}             |
|                                  |
|o13 : ForeignObject of type char**|
+----------------------------------+
* Menu:

* foreignPointerArrayType::     construct a foreign pointer array type
* ForeignPointerArrayType VisibleList::  cast a Macaulay2 list to a foreign pointer array

