determined automatically based on type of the input. Integers are converted to
*note int32: ForeignIntegerType, objects.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : foreignObject 5            |
|                                |
|o1 = 5                          |
|                                |
|o1 : ForeignObject of type int32|
+--------------------------------+

Non-integers are converted to *note double: ForeignRealType, objects.

+---------------------------------+
|i2 : foreignObject pi            |
|                                 |
|o2 = 3.141592653589793           |
|                                 |
|o2 : ForeignObject of type double|
+---------------------------------+

Strings are converted to *note charstar: ForeignStringType, objects.

+----------------------------------+
|i3 : foreignObject "Hello, world!"|
|                                  |
|o3 = Hello, world!                |
|                                  |
|o3 : ForeignObject of type char*  |
+----------------------------------+

Pointers are converted to *note voidstar: ForeignPointerType, objects.

+--------------------------------+
|i4 : foreignObject nullPointer  |
|                                |
|o4 = (nil)                      |
|                                |
|o4 : ForeignObject of type void*|
+--------------------------------+

Lists are converted to foreign objects with the appropriate *note
ForeignArrayType: ForeignArrayType,.

+-----------------------------------+
|i5 : foreignObject {1, 3, 5, 7, 9} |
|                                   |
|o5 = {1, 3, 5, 7, 9}               |
|                                   |
|o5 : ForeignObject of type int32[5]|
+-----------------------------------+

No conversion is done when the input is already a foreign object.

+-----------------------------------+
|i6 : foreignObject oo              |
|                                   |
|o6 = {1, 3, 5, 7, 9}               |
|                                   |
|o6 : ForeignObject of type int32[5]|
+-----------------------------------+

Ways to use foreignObject:
==========================

  * "foreignObject(ForeignObject)"
  * "foreignObject(Number)"
  * "foreignObject(Pointer)"
  * "foreignObject(String)"
  * "foreignObject(VisibleList)"
  * "foreignObject(ZZ)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note foreignObject: foreignObject, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

