foreignSymbol -- get a foreign symbol
*************************************

  * Usage: 
        foreignSymbol(lib, symb, T)
        foreignSymbol(symb, T)
  * Inputs:
      * lib, a *note shared library: SharedLibrary,, 
      * symb, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 
      * T, a *note foreign type: ForeignType,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note foreign object: ForeignObject,, 

Description
===========

This function is a wrapper around the C function dlsym.  It loads a symbol from
a shared library using the specified foreign type. If the shared library is
already linked against Macaulay2, then it may be omitted.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : foreignSymbol("errno", int)|
|                                |
|o1 = 0                          |
|                                |
|o1 : ForeignObject of type int32|
+--------------------------------+

Ways to use foreignSymbol:
==========================

  * "foreignSymbol(SharedLibrary,String,ForeignType)"
  * "foreignSymbol(String,ForeignType)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note foreignSymbol: foreignSymbol, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

