File: ForeignFunctions.info, Node: value_lpForeignObject_rp, Next: ForeignType ForeignObject, Prev: foreignSymbol, Up: ForeignObject

value(ForeignObject) -- get the value of a foreign object as a Macaulay2 thing
******************************************************************************

  * Function: *note value: (Macaulay2Doc)value,
  * Usage: 
        value x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note foreign object: ForeignObject,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, 

Description
===========

Convert the given foreign object to the corresponding Macaulay2 thing. The type
of the output is determined by the type of the foreign object. Foreign integer
objects are converted to *note ZZ: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, objects.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : x = int 5                  |
|                                |
|o1 = 5                          |
|                                |
|o1 : ForeignObject of type int32|
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : value x                    |
|                                |
|o2 = 5                          |
+--------------------------------+

Foreign real objects are converted to *note RR: (Macaulay2Doc)RR, objects.

+---------------------------------+
|i3 : x = double 5                |
|                                 |
|o3 = 5                           |
|                                 |
|o3 : ForeignObject of type double|
+---------------------------------+
|i4 : value x                     |
|                                 |
|o4 = 5                           |
|                                 |
|o4 : RR (of precision 53)        |
+---------------------------------+

Foreign pointer objects are converted to *note Pointer: Pointer, objects.

+--------------------------------+
|i5 : x = voidstar address int 5 |
|                                |
|o5 = 0x7fb3b71827f0             |
|                                |
|o5 : ForeignObject of type void*|
+--------------------------------+
|i6 : value x                    |
|                                |
|o6 = 0x7fb3b71827f0             |
|                                |
|o6 : Pointer                    |
+--------------------------------+

Foreign string objects are converted to strings.

+---------------------------------+
|i7 : x = charstar "Hello, world!"|
|                                 |
|o7 = Hello, world!               |
|                                 |
|o7 : ForeignObject of type char* |
+---------------------------------+
|i8 : value x                     |
|                                 |
|o8 = Hello, world!               |
+---------------------------------+

Foreign array objects are converted to lists.

+-----------------------------------+
|i9 : x = (4 * int) {2, 4, 6, 8}    |
|                                   |
|o9 = {2, 4, 6, 8}                  |
|                                   |
|o9 : ForeignObject of type int32[4]|
+-----------------------------------+
|i10 : value x                      |
|                                   |
|o10 = {2, 4, 6, 8}                 |
|                                   |
|o10 : List                         |
+-----------------------------------+

Foreign struct and union objects are converted to hash tables.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : mystruct = foreignStructType("mystruct", {"a" => int, "b" => float})|
|                                                                          |
|o11 = mystruct                                                            |
|                                                                          |
|o11 : ForeignStructType                                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : x = mystruct {"a" => 2, "b" => sqrt 2}                              |
|                                                                          |
|o12 = HashTable{"a" => 2      }                                           |
|                "b" => 1.41421                                            |
|                                                                          |
|o12 : ForeignObject of type mystruct                                      |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : value x                                                             |
|                                                                          |
|o13 = HashTable{"a" => 2      }                                           |
|                "b" => 1.41421                                            |
|                                                                          |
|o13 : HashTable                                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Note that this function is also used by *note describe:
(Macaulay2Doc)describe,, *note expression: (Macaulay2Doc)expression,, *note
net: (Macaulay2Doc)net,, *note texMath: (Macaulay2Doc)texMath,, *note
toExternalString: (Macaulay2Doc)toExternalString,, and *note toString:
(Macaulay2Doc)toString, for representing foreign objects.

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "value(charstar)"
  * "value(charstarstar)"
  * "value(double)"
  * "value(float)"
  * *note value(ForeignObject): value_lpForeignObject_rp, -- get the value of a
    foreign object as a Macaulay2 thing
  * "value(int8)"
  * "value(int16)"
  * "value(int32)"
  * "value(int64)"
  * "value(uint8)"
  * "value(uint16)"
  * "value(uint32)"
  * "value(uint64)"
  * "value(voidstar)"
  * "value(voidstarstar)"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

