Pointer -- pointer to memory address
************************************

Description
===========

Pointer objects are pointers to memory addresses.  These make up each *note
ForeignObject: ForeignObject,.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : x = int 20                      |
|                                     |
|o1 = 20                              |
|                                     |
|o1 : ForeignObject of type int32     |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : peek x                          |
|                                     |
|o2 = int32{Address => 0x7fb3b7182f50}|
+-------------------------------------+

These pointers can be accessed using *note address: address,.

+--------------------+
|i3 : ptr = address x|
|                    |
|o3 = 0x7fb3b7182f50 |
|                    |
|o3 : Pointer        |
+--------------------+

Simple arithmetic can be performed on pointers.

+-------------------+
|i4 : ptr + 5       |
|                   |
|o4 = 0x7fb3b7182f55|
|                   |
|o4 : Pointer       |
+-------------------+
|i5 : ptr - 3       |
|                   |
|o5 = 0x7fb3b7182f4d|
|                   |
|o5 : Pointer       |
+-------------------+
* Menu:

* nullPointer::                 the null pointer
* address::                     pointer to type or object
* ForeignType Pointer::         dereference a pointer

Functions and methods returning a pointer:
==========================================

  * *note address: address, -- pointer to type or object

Methods that use a pointer:
===========================

  * "* Pointer = Thing" -- see *note * voidstar = Thing: _st voidstar = Thing,
    -- assign value to object at address
  * "foreignFunction(Pointer,String,ForeignType,VisibleList)" -- see *note
    foreignFunction: foreignFunction, -- construct a foreign function
  * "foreignObject(Pointer)" -- see *note foreignObject: foreignObject, --
    construct a foreign object
  * *note ForeignPointerType Pointer: ForeignPointerType Pointer, -- cast a
    Macaulay2 pointer to a foreign pointer
  * *note ForeignType Pointer: ForeignType Pointer, -- dereference a pointer
  * "Pointer + ZZ"
  * "Pointer - ZZ"
  * "ZZ + Pointer"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note Pointer: Pointer, is a *note type: (Macaulay2Doc)Type,, with
ancestor class *note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

